ai_engine.py (2)
346-362: Replace busy-wait loop with asyncio.Event for better concurrency.

The busy-wait pattern while self._initializing: await asyncio.sleep(0.1) is inefficient and can cause unnecessary delays and CPU usage under high concurrency. Multiple callers will repeatedly wake up and check the flag every 100ms.

Replace the busy-wait with an asyncio.Event:

     def __init__(self):
         self.device = torch.device("cuda" if torch.cuda.is_available() else "cpu")
         print(f"🤖 AI Engine using device: {self.device}")
         
         # ... existing code ...
         
         # Initialization flags
         self._initialized = False
-        self._initializing = False
+        self._init_event = asyncio.Event()
+        self._init_event.set()  # Initially ready to initialize

     async def ensure_initialized(self):
         """Stellt sicher, dass die Initialisierung durchgeführt wurde"""
         if self._initialized:
             return

-        if self._initializing:
-            # Warte, bis die Initialisierung abgeschlossen ist
-            while self._initializing:
-                await asyncio.sleep(0.1)
-            return
-
-        self._initializing = True
+        # Wait for permission to initialize (only one caller proceeds)
+        await self._init_event.wait()
+        
+        # Double-check after acquiring the event
+        if self._initialized:
+            return
+            
+        self._init_event.clear()  # Block other callers
         try:
             await self.load_models()
             self._initialized = True
         finally:
-            self._initializing = False
+            self._init_event.set()  # Unblock waiting callers
This ensures only one initialization runs while others efficiently wait without polling.

